 * **`IO::sync_parent_dir`** is a new required method on the `IO` trait (an **IO extension**; see [docs/adr/0001-io-extensions-are-required-trait-methods.md](docs/adr/0001-io-extensions-are-required-trait-methods.md)). It makes a file's directory entry durable. Out-of-tree `IO` implementations must now implement it; an IO that cannot provide it returns `LimboError::IoExtensionUnsupported`, and `OrphanWalPolicy::Discard` then refuses to open an empty database on it.
 * **GitHub-hosted CI.** CI runs on GitHub-hosted runners instead of Blacksmith, and jobs that need upstream secrets or publish/deploy run only in `tursodatabase/turso`.
 * **Bound parameters are shared, not copied.** Bound Text and Blob parameters are shared with the registers that read them instead of copied, so binding a parameter and reading it (even several times, or again after `Statement::reset`) no longer copies its payload. Serializing the value into the record is the only copy, unless an instruction has to change the value (for example, when column affinity turns the text `'42'` into an integer).
+* **`DELETE ... ORDER BY` / `DELETE ... LIMIT` errors name the clause.** Like upstream, these statements are refused at parse time and delete nothing, but the error says why: `near "ORDER": syntax error: ORDER BY clause is not supported in DELETE`, or `near "LIMIT": syntax error: LIMIT clause is not supported in DELETE`. Upstream reports only `near "ORDER": syntax error`.
 
